Package: lighthouse
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: LightHouse <support@lighthouse.local>
Homepage: https://github.com/gotsevrossen/LightHouse
# The WebKitGTK runtime pywebview renders the dashboard in. Ubuntu 22.04 ships
# the 4.0 ABI and 24.04 ships 4.1, so both are listed as alternatives rather than
# pinning one and making the package uninstallable on the other release. python3-gi
# and the GIR data are what pywebview's GTK backend imports at runtime; the WebKit
# library alone does not pull them in.
#
# No ${misc:Depends}: that is a debhelper substitution variable, and this package
# is assembled with dpkg-deb directly, which would ship it through unexpanded.
Depends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 | libwebkit2gtk-4.0-37,
         gir1.2-webkit2-4.1 | gir1.2-webkit2-4.0,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         curl,
         gnupg,
         software-properties-common,
         adduser,
         python3
# Suricata, Zeek, Wazuh and Ollama are deliberately NOT dependencies: they come
# from third-party repositories that apt does not know about until postinst adds
# them, so declaring them here would make this package uninstallable.
Description: LightHouse local AI security copilot
 LightHouse turns local Suricata, Zeek, and Wazuh records into validated,
 plain-English security guidance. Monitoring data and AI inference stay on
 this machine; nothing is sent to a remote service.
 .
 Monitoring runs as a background service from boot. The desktop window is a
 viewer onto it, so closing the window does not stop protection.
